WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.942
You want to investigate the open access

00:00:02.962 --> 00:00:04.462
citation advantage.

00:00:04.611 --> 00:00:06.756
You could type a question, choose a known

00:00:06.776 --> 00:00:09.527
paper, follow a citation, or give a

00:00:09.547 --> 00:00:11.433
controller a research brief.

00:00:11.583 --> 00:00:13.728
Are these four ways of phrasing the same

00:00:13.748 --> 00:00:15.738
query? Pause and predict.

00:00:18.146 --> 00:00:20.547
They address different mechanisms.

00:00:20.722 --> 00:00:22.983
A query represents the need in a form a

00:00:23.003 --> 00:00:24.503
system can act on.

00:00:24.679 --> 00:00:27.120
Changing from words to a seed paper or

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:29.941
citation changes more than the wording.

00:00:30.872 --> 00:00:33.469
A free text string might go to lexical,

00:00:33.503 --> 00:00:35.570
dense or hybrid retrieval.

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:37.890
The visible box does not reveal whether

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:41.202
words will be analysed, encoded, rewritten

00:00:41.222 --> 00:00:44.114
or routed. A controlled term or structured

00:00:44.134 --> 00:00:47.323
expression addresses annotations, fields,

00:00:47.343 --> 00:00:49.758
filters or Boolean conditions.

00:00:50.298 --> 00:00:53.381
A MeSH heading, field tag or tested search

00:00:53.401 --> 00:00:56.035
hedge is not simply a formal keyword.

00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:57.879
It depends on the target database’s

00:00:57.899 --> 00:01:00.442
structure and supported syntax.

00:01:01.342 --> 00:01:03.808
A seed document makes a known paper stand

00:01:03.828 --> 00:01:05.934
for the need. The system might compare its

00:01:05.954 --> 00:01:08.975
text, follow citation relationships, or

00:01:08.995 --> 00:01:11.836
combine both. PubMed Similar Articles, for

00:01:11.856 --> 00:01:14.517
example, uses a word weighted approach

00:01:14.537 --> 00:01:17.867
over title, abstract and MeSH words; a

00:01:17.887 --> 00:01:19.839
seed does not automatically imply

00:01:19.859 --> 00:01:20.805
embeddings.

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:23.244
Citation methods differ too.

00:01:23.419 --> 00:01:26.891
Direct traversal follows explicit citation

00:01:26.911 --> 00:01:30.422
edges. Bibliographic coupling finds papers

00:01:30.442 --> 00:01:31.852
sharing references.

00:01:32.014 --> 00:01:34.996
Co citation finds papers cited together.

00:01:35.159 --> 00:01:36.659
Their reach depends on the graph’s

00:01:36.679 --> 00:01:38.902
coverage and timing, rather than only on

00:01:38.922 --> 00:01:40.486
the searcher’s vocabulary.

00:01:41.409 --> 00:01:43.690
A relevance judgement can help construct a

00:01:43.710 --> 00:01:46.319
later retrieval input from accepted or

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.633
rejected records.

00:01:47.808 --> 00:01:50.417
Pseudo relevance feedback instead assumes

00:01:50.437 --> 00:01:53.381
highly ranked records are useful without

00:01:53.401 --> 00:01:54.734
asking the searcher.

00:01:55.284 --> 00:01:58.211
A browse or monitoring target addresses a

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:01.600
journal, author, subject, collection or

00:02:01.620 --> 00:02:02.746
continuing alert.

00:02:02.908 --> 00:02:05.272
It can surface a paper you recognise as

00:02:05.292 --> 00:02:08.288
useful even when you could not have named

00:02:08.308 --> 00:02:11.020
it in advance. These are different ways

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:12.295
into the literature.

00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:15.202
A programmatic predicate can specify

00:02:15.222 --> 00:02:19.120
identifiers, ranges, filtering, sorting

00:02:19.140 --> 00:02:20.305
and pagination.

00:02:20.454 --> 00:02:23.231
OpenAlex documents composable attribute

00:02:23.251 --> 00:02:26.440
filters. A task brief instead gives a

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:29.287
controller scope, inclusion criteria,

00:02:29.333 --> 00:02:31.981
sources, stopping conditions and output

00:02:32.001 --> 00:02:34.648
requirements. Those instructions are not

00:02:34.668 --> 00:02:37.251
all terms that an underlying retriever can

00:02:37.271 --> 00:02:38.037
obey.

00:02:38.609 --> 00:02:41.009
Even a filter needs the right meaning.

00:02:41.210 --> 00:02:43.020
Filtering results to papers that are

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:45.958
themselves open access could exclude a

00:02:45.978 --> 00:02:48.561
paywalled study about the open access

00:02:48.581 --> 00:02:50.004
citation advantage.

00:02:50.192 --> 00:02:52.711
The chapter’s example therefore filters by

00:02:52.731 --> 00:02:54.450
publication year instead.

00:02:55.368 --> 00:02:56.943
These objects cooperate.

00:02:57.119 --> 00:02:59.895
Text and controlled vocabulary can find

00:02:59.915 --> 00:03:02.936
seeds; citation traversal can expose

00:03:02.956 --> 00:03:05.617
missing terminology; accepted records can

00:03:05.637 --> 00:03:08.542
guide feedback; an API can make a

00:03:08.562 --> 00:03:09.998
procedure repeatable.

00:03:10.173 --> 00:03:12.485
Bates called developing a search through

00:03:12.505 --> 00:03:14.624
such discoveries berrypicking.

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:17.990
In one audit of a single complex evidence

00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:20.645
review, researchers traced four hundred

00:03:20.665 --> 00:03:23.260
ninety five included sources.

00:03:23.461 --> 00:03:26.392
Thirty percent came from protocol defined

00:03:26.412 --> 00:03:29.111
database and hand searches, and fifty one

00:03:29.131 --> 00:03:30.734
percent from snowballing.

00:03:30.909 --> 00:03:33.364
That is a scoped example, not a universal

00:03:33.384 --> 00:03:34.858
estimate for reviews.

00:03:35.744 --> 00:03:38.214
When the query really is text, useful

00:03:38.234 --> 00:03:40.159
wording depends on its receiver.

00:03:40.322 --> 00:03:43.562
A lexical engine needs observable concepts

00:03:43.582 --> 00:03:45.211
and supported operators.

00:03:45.373 --> 00:03:47.866
A dense retriever needs a description

00:03:47.886 --> 00:03:49.747
suited to what its model was trained to

00:03:49.767 --> 00:03:53.046
match. Longer prose is not automatically

00:03:53.066 --> 00:03:53.716
better.

00:03:54.261 --> 00:03:57.189
A query translator needs enough context to

00:03:57.209 --> 00:04:00.087
produce inspectable retrieval inputs.

00:04:00.276 --> 00:04:02.846
Detailed relevance instructions do not

00:04:02.866 --> 00:04:05.075
automatically become instructions followed

00:04:05.095 --> 00:04:08.516
by every retrieval model; that capability

00:04:08.536 --> 00:04:09.868
depends on training.

00:04:10.770 --> 00:04:13.712
If the architecture is undisclosed, vary

00:04:13.732 --> 00:04:15.955
inputs systematically against known

00:04:15.975 --> 00:04:19.356
relevant records: short terms, a question,

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:22.217
fielded syntax and a known item title.

00:04:22.353 --> 00:04:25.220
Inspect generated expressions for valid

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:28.029
fields, controlled terms and logical

00:04:28.049 --> 00:04:30.567
relationships in the target database.

00:04:31.123 --> 00:04:33.722
Generated Boolean strategies can contain

00:04:33.742 --> 00:04:35.848
invalid MeSH terms.

00:04:36.010 --> 00:04:38.039
A polished paragraph is no quality

00:04:38.059 --> 00:04:41.067
guarantee. Start with the query object and

00:04:41.087 --> 00:04:43.310
receiving mechanism, then test what the

00:04:43.330 --> 00:04:45.100
system actually does.
